<title>JAPAN: S&amp;P assigns AA to W.Australian Treasury's samurais.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P assigns AA to W.Australian Treasury's samurais.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard and Poor's Corp said on Friday it had assigned an AA rating to Western Australian Treasury Corp's 20 billion yen worth of 4.8 percent yen/U.S. dollar dual currency samurai bonds due on March 16, 2000.</p>
<p>S&amp;P said in a statement that the rating reflected that of its guarantor, the state of Western Australia.</p>
<p>It also said that the rating was constrained by the AA foreign currency sovereign rating of Australia.</p>
<p>It said the outlook for the rating was positive.</p>
</text>
